      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rockland sprang up around the Victoria Mine, where log cabins built in 1899 housed waves of copper miners and their families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/old-victoria.htm",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "At Old Victoria, visitors can tour four historically furnished homes and hear stories of the town’s early residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/old-victoria.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Sanborn Fire Insurance Maps from 1902 and 1917 reveal Rockland’s downtown layout, labeled businesses, schools, and other landmarks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://hometownhistorymaps.com/pages/history-of-rockland-michigan",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Online collections of Rockland’s Sanborn maps let researchers compare how the town changed between 1902 and 1917.",
